# Non-verifiable judge benchmark — tasks with no executable oracle (explain/factual/reason/summarize/instruct).
# Ground truth by construction: see prompts_nonverifiable_refs.jsonl (reference=correct, mutant=one labeled defect).
{"id": "explain-altitude-boiling", "prompt": "Explain why water boils at a lower temperature at high altitudes than it does at sea level.", "bucket": "explain", "tier": "easy", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "explain-rainbow-colors", "prompt": "Explain how a rainbow forms and why its colors appear in the order they do (which color is on the outer edge and which on the inner edge).", "bucket": "explain", "tier": "medium", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "explain-blue-sky", "prompt": "Explain why the daytime sky appears blue.", "bucket": "explain", "tier": "medium", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "explain-mrna-vaccine", "prompt": "Explain how mRNA vaccines (such as those developed for COVID-19) train the immune system.", "bucket": "explain", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "explain-greenhouse-effect", "prompt": "Explain the mechanism by which greenhouse gases warm the Earth's surface.", "bucket": "explain", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "explain-sailing-upwind", "prompt": "Explain how a sailboat can make progress in a direction that has a component toward the wind (upwind), rather than only being pushed along downwind.", "bucket": "explain", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "factual-fastest-land-animal", "prompt": "What is the fastest land animal, and roughly how fast can it run at top speed?", "bucket": "factual", "tier": "easy", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "factual-adult-bone-count", "prompt": "How many bones are in the adult human body, and how does that number compare to the number a baby is born with?", "bucket": "factual", "tier": "medium", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "factual-deepest-ocean", "prompt": "What is the deepest known point in Earth's oceans, and approximately how deep is it?", "bucket": "factual", "tier": "medium", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "factual-olympus-mons", "prompt": "What is the tallest known mountain or volcano in the Solar System, where is it located, and roughly how tall is it?", "bucket": "factual", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "factual-speed-of-sound", "prompt": "Roughly how fast does sound travel through air, and what is one key factor that changes that speed?", "bucket": "factual", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "factual-dna-base-pairs", "prompt": "In DNA's double helix, which bases pair with which, and how do the two kinds of base pair differ in the number of hydrogen bonds holding them together?", "bucket": "factual", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "reason-shortest-of-three", "prompt": "Alice is taller than Bob, and Bob is taller than Carol. Of the three, who is the shortest? Explain your reasoning.", "bucket": "reason", "tier": "easy", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "reason-jacket-discount-tax", "prompt": "A jacket has a list price of $80. A store first applies a 25% discount, and then 10% sales tax is added to the discounted price. What is the final price the customer pays? Show your reasoning.", "bucket": "reason", "tier": "medium", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "reason-trains-meet", "prompt": "Town A and Town B are 300 miles apart along a straight road. A train leaves Town A heading toward Town B at 50 mph at 1:00 pm. A second train leaves Town B heading toward Town A at 70 mph at 2:00 pm. At what clock time do the two trains meet? Explain.", "bucket": "reason", "tier": "medium", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "reason-pipes-tank", "prompt": "An empty tank can be filled by pipe A in 4 hours and by pipe B in 6 hours. A drain, pipe C, can empty a full tank in 12 hours. If all three are opened at once on an empty tank, how long does it take to fill the tank? Show your reasoning.", "bucket": "reason", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "reason-father-son-age", "prompt": "A father is currently three times as old as his son. In 12 years, the father will be twice as old as his son will be then. How old is the son now? Show your reasoning.", "bucket": "reason", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "reason-two-red-marbles", "prompt": "A bag contains 5 red marbles and 3 blue marbles. You draw two marbles at random, one after the other, without replacing the first before drawing the second. What is the probability that both marbles are red? Show your reasoning.", "bucket": "reason", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "summarize-lunch-walk-study", "prompt": "Summarize the main finding of the following passage in one sentence, staying faithful to what it actually claims:\n\nA small observational study followed 200 office workers over six months. Participants who took a 10-minute walk after lunch reported feeling slightly more alert in the afternoon than those who stayed seated. The researchers noted the effect was modest and that participants were not randomly assigned. They cautioned that the results might simply reflect other healthy habits of people who choose to walk. Larger controlled trials would be needed to confirm any real benefit.", "bucket": "summarize", "tier": "easy", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "summarize-coral-currents", "prompt": "Summarize the key finding and conclusion of the following passage in one or two sentences, faithful to the source:\n\nResearchers surveyed a reef system over a decade. They found that reefs located near strong ocean currents recovered from bleaching faster than reefs in calmer waters. The team suggested that currents may deliver cooler water and disperse accumulated heat. However, reefs near currents were also more exposed to physical storm damage. The authors concluded that the relationship between water movement and reef health is complex and not simply positive.", "bucket": "summarize", "tier": "medium", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "summarize-hybrid-work", "prompt": "Summarize what the following report found, in one or two sentences, including only claims the passage supports:\n\nA company reviewed productivity after shifting to a hybrid schedule in which employees came to the office three days a week. Managers reported that project deadlines were met at roughly the same rate as before the change. Survey responses showed employees valued the flexibility and reported lower commuting stress. The report did not measure any change in overall company revenue.", "bucket": "summarize", "tier": "medium", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "summarize-sleep-memory", "prompt": "Summarize the main result of the following passage in one sentence, staying faithful to the strength of the claim:\n\nIn a laboratory experiment, 40 volunteers memorized word lists and were tested after either a full night's sleep or a night of restricted sleep. On average, the well-rested group recalled more words. The difference was statistically significant but small in absolute terms. The authors noted that all participants were healthy young adults, so the findings may not extend to older populations. They described the result as consistent with, but not proof of, a causal role for sleep in memory consolidation.", "bucket": "summarize", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "summarize-battery-electrode", "prompt": "Summarize the main finding of the following passage in one or two sentences, faithful to the source:\n\nEngineers tested a new battery electrode in the laboratory. In early cells, the electrode retained 90 percent of its capacity after 1,000 charge cycles, better than the current standard. However, the tests used small coin-sized cells under carefully controlled temperatures. The team has not yet built full-sized batteries or tested performance in real devices. They estimate several years of development remain before any commercial use.", "bucket": "summarize", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "summarize-bilingual-vocab", "prompt": "Summarize the main finding of the following passage in one or two sentences, faithful to the source:\n\nA linguist analyzed how children in a bilingual community acquired their two languages. Children exposed to both languages from birth reached typical vocabulary milestones in each language slightly later than monolingual peers. But when the vocabularies of both languages were counted together, the bilingual children knew as many words overall. The study found no evidence that bilingualism delayed general cognitive development. The author framed the early single-language lag as a normal feature of distributing learning across two systems.", "bucket": "summarize", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "instruct-formal-reschedule", "prompt": "Rewrite the following sentence to be more formal and professional while keeping its meaning exactly the same: \"Hey, we can't make the Tuesday meeting work, so let's push it to next week.\"", "bucket": "instruct", "tier": "easy", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "instruct-kyoto-two-part", "prompt": "A friend messages: \"I'm visiting Kyoto for the first time in mid-November. What should I pack for the weather, and are there any etiquette rules I should know before visiting the temples?\" Answer both parts of their question.", "bucket": "instruct", "tier": "medium", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "instruct-complaint-no-liability", "prompt": "Write a reply to this customer email, apologizing for the customer's frustration and offering a resolution, but without admitting that the company was at fault or legally liable: \"Your blender stopped working after just three weeks and leaked all over my counter. This is unacceptable and I want it sorted out immediately.\"", "bucket": "instruct", "tier": "medium", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "instruct-feedback-no-attack", "prompt": "Give a new manager concrete advice on how to deliver honest, specific critical feedback to an underperforming employee while avoiding language that attacks the person's character or leaves them feeling demoralized.", "bucket": "instruct", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "instruct-compound-gap-accelerates", "prompt": "A student writes: \"I already understand why compound interest grows faster than simple interest. What I don't understand is why the gap between the two keeps widening faster and faster over time instead of growing by the same amount each year. Explain that specifically.\"", "bucket": "instruct", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
{"id": "instruct-antibiotic-handling", "prompt": "Explain to a parent, in plain everyday language, how to correctly handle their child's liquid antibiotic at home. Convey all of the important instructions: it must be kept in the refrigerator, shaken well before every dose, measured with the syringe provided (not a kitchen spoon), given until the full course is finished even if the child seems better, and thrown away 10 days after it was mixed.", "bucket": "instruct", "tier": "hard", "verify": "judgment"}
